    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d17">

                <pb facs="0105" n="15" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg15"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/1702: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >White</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-17T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17, 1920—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>114. Minister Céspedes has suggested the advisability of submitting to President
                    Menocal a statement to be given out by him to the Cuban people, which embodies
                    the points made in Department’s instruction of June 4th. Rough draft proposed
                    statement being sent for your information.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d17-f1"/>
                    Should same be published last paragraph instruction under discussion might be
                    disregarded.</p>
                <p>If nothing develops by middle next week you might inquire what impression was
                    produced by Minister Céspedes’ proposal.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
